                <pb facs="0531" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.01/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-08T10:00:00-05:00">November 8, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>82. Your November 5, 11 a.m. You will today, but not earlier than 2 hours from
                    this time, answer the note of November 3d from the Brazilian Government by
                    stating “that this Government will be happy to continue with the new Government
                    the same friendly relations as with its predecessors.”</p>
                <p>You will at once confidentially advise your British, Colombian and Cuban
                    colleagues what your instructions are.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
